----------------\nAffine Mendelsohn triple systems and the Eisenstein integers (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/jcd.21739)\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # Affine Mendelsohn triple systems and the Eisenstein integers ... Nowak, ... We also prove that for any affine MTS, the qualities of being nonramified, pure, and self-orthogonal are equivalent.\n\nVolume 28, Issue 10 pp. 724-744\n\nRESEARCH ARTICLE\n\n# Affine Mendelsohn triple systems and the Eisenstein integers\n\nAlex W. Nowak, \n\nCorresponding Author\n\nAlex W. Nowak\n\n  * anowak@iastate.edu\n  * alexwn1212@gmail.com\n\n  * orcid.org/0000-0001-5914-914X\n\nDepartment of Mathematics, Iowa State University, Ames, Iowa\n\nCorrespondence Alex W. Nowak, Department of Mathematics, Iowa State University, Ames, IA 50011.\n\nEmail: anowak@iastate.edu and alexwn1212@gmail.com\n\nSearch for more papers by this author\n\nFirst published: 24 June 2020\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1002/jcd.21739Digital Object Identifier (DOI)\n\nview metrics\n\nRead the full text\n\n  * References\n\n### Abstract\n\nWe define a Mendelsohn triple system (MTS) of order coprime with 3, and having multiplication affine over an abelian group, to be affine, nonramified. By exhibiting a one-to-one correspondence between isomorphism classes of affine MTS and those of modules over the Eisenstein integers, we solve the isomorphism problem for affine, nonramified MTS and enumerate these isomorphism classes (extending the work of Donovan, Griggs, McCourt, Opršal, and Stanovský). As a consequence, all entropic MTSs of order coprime with 3 and distributive MTS of order coprime with 3 are classified. Partial results on the isomorphism problem for affine MTS with order divisible by 3 are given, and a complete classification is conjectured. We also prove that for any affine MTS, the qualities of being nonramified, pure, and self-orthogonal are equivalent.\n\nOctober 2020\n\nPages 724-744\n\n### How to cite\n\nNowak AW. Affine Mendelsohn triple systems and the Eisenstein integers. J Combin Des. 2020; 27: 724–744. https://doi.org/10.1002/jcd.21739\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1154-05-1730 (https://jointmathematicsmeetings.org/amsmtgs/2245_abstracts/1154-05-1730.pdf)\nciteturn2search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Alex W Nowak* (anowak@iastate.edu), 396 Carver Hall, 411 Morrill Road, Ames, IA 50011. ... We study Mendelsohn triple systems whose quasigroup multiplication is self-distributive; that is, x(yz) = (xy)(xz),\n1154-05-1730\nAlex W Nowak* (anowak@iastate.edu), 396 Carver Hall, 411 Morrill Road, Ames, IA 50011.\nDistributive Mendelsohn triple systems and the Eisenstein integers.\nWe study Mendelsohn triple systems whose quasigroup multiplication is self-distributive; that is, x(yz) = (xy)(xz),\n(zy)x = (zx)(yx). Building on the work of Donovan et al. we give a direct product decomposition for any such system\nwhose point set has order coprime with 3. This allows for a complete description and enumeration of isomorphism classes.\nWe present the complications related to the case in which the point set is divisible by 3. (Received September 16, 2019)\n1--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHartford Divorces vol 106 (https://portal.ct.gov/-/media/CSL/departments/reference-services/PDFs/Hartford-County-Divorce-Index/Hartford-Index-vol-106-1948.pdf)\nciteturn2search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.8 years ago; Crawled: 9.5 years ago; | Mendelsohn, Olive Parsons | v. ... | Nowak Anne Ostrowski | v. ... | Leslie R. | 438 (handwritten correction: 437) |\nIndex of Cases — M, N, O\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n\n| Plaintiff | v. | Defendant | Page |\n|---|---|---|---:|\n| Mendelsohn, Olive Parsons | v. | Gebhard | 733 |\n| Marsh Frances Guy | v. | Ben F. | 740 |\n| Morris Helen Mary | v. | Charles W. | 744 |\n| Maddoux Ethel Richards Lee | v. | Alonzo alias |